  "prefLabel": "En 1005.02 Utility TIRs",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1005.02 Utility TIRs. Each utility shall publish and maintain TIRs. The utilities shall convene a TIR working group quarterly that includes participation from interested stakeholders to ensure technical standards are regularly maintained, updated, and consistent with good utility practice. The TIR working group shall be comprised of 6 members with 3 members representing utilities and 3 members representing companies engaged in the development and installation of DERs in New Hampshire. The TIR working group shall have 2 co-chairs with one representing utility members and one representing industry members. The utilities shall provide notice of changes to the TIR working group.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
